{"availability":"available","full":"kstrat2001/darkmux","name":"darkmux","description":"Mission orchestrator and lab for local AI. Launch a mission, watch the graph come alive — every seat runs your own models off the meter, or a hosted endpoint.","category":"Developer tools","language":"Rust","stars":8,"forks":1,"created":"2026-05-09T18:33:00Z","updated":"2026-10-15T14:56:21Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://darkmux.com","topics":["agent-tooling","apple-silicon","cli","llm","lmstudio","local-ai","rust"],"demo":"https://darkmux.com/demo","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-15T15:02:12.529Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-15T15:02:12.529Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-15T15:02:12.529Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-11T07:26:46.051Z","stars":7,"forks":1},{"at":"2026-10-15T15:02:12.529Z","stars":8,"forks":1}],"technologies":["Rust"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Own your AI workforce. Run real engineering work on models you already have, on machines you already own.","darkmux turns a Mac (or a few of them on a tailnet) into a working local-AI fleet: config-defined missions run as live task graphs by a crew of role-staffed models. Every consequential step gates on your sign-off. Every dispatch leaves a record: which machine, which model, and why. Underneath it, a lab that measures what your hardware actually does, so your configuration rests on numbers, not vibes.","darkmux.com · Live demo — watch a real mission replay in your browser. Nothing to install."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/kstrat2001/darkmux/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"f9c72cca444cf2cd2e6e4c213f805741776e8f234f40d52b06cde003726eaa8a","extractedAt":"2026-10-15T15:02:12.694Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-15T15:02:12.694Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Own your AI workforce. Run real engineering work on models you already have, on machines you already own.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/kstrat2001/darkmux